    "title": "Chronic tension-type headache",
    "conclusion": "Chronic tension-type headache without red flags; NICE CG150 says to consider a course of up to 10 acupuncture sessions over 5–8 weeks for prophylaxis. Note the analgesic use (about 10 days a month): a medication-overuse review with her doctor is worthwhile.",
    "keyReasoning": [
      "Bilateral pressing headache without nausea or red flags; normal neurology."
    ],
    "teachingPoints": [
      "Never needle GB20 deeply upwards and medially, nor GB21 deeply perpendicular.",
